## 4. Booking And Payment Sequence Diagram

Description: Shows the main end-to-end business flow from booking creation to payment confirmation and driver assignment.

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    actor Farmer
    participant UI as Farmer Dashboard
    participant BookingAPI as Booking API
    participant Maps as Maps Service
    participant DB as Database
    participant PaymentAPI as Payments API
    participant Daraja as Safaricom Daraja
    actor Driver
    participant DriverAPI as Driver APIs

    Farmer->>UI: Enter produce, pickup, dropoff
    UI->>Maps: Preview route / resolve places
    Maps-->>UI: Distance, duration, geometry
    UI->>BookingAPI: Create booking
    BookingAPI->>DB: Save booking as pending_payment
    DB-->>BookingAPI: Booking created
    BookingAPI-->>UI: Quote, vehicle type, matched transporters

    Farmer->>UI: Start payment
    UI->>PaymentAPI: POST /api/payments/stk-push/
    PaymentAPI->>Daraja: Initiate STK Push
    Daraja-->>PaymentAPI: STK request accepted
    PaymentAPI->>DB: Save payment as stk_push_sent
    PaymentAPI-->>UI: Prompt user to complete payment

    Daraja->>PaymentAPI: Payment callback
    PaymentAPI->>DB: Mark payment paid_held
    PaymentAPI->>DB: Mark booking confirmed / paid

    Driver->>DriverAPI: Load open jobs
    DriverAPI->>DB: Query confirmed + matching jobs
    DB-->>DriverAPI: Matching bookings
    DriverAPI-->>Driver: Show available jobs

    Driver->>DriverAPI: Accept booking with vehicle
    DriverAPI->>DB: Assign transporter + vehicle
    DriverAPI->>DB: Update booking to accepted
    DriverAPI-->>Driver: Booking accepted
```

## 5. Delivery Execution Sequence Diagram

Description: Shows how the assigned driver progresses the trip from pickup to delivery and how payout release logic is triggered.

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    actor Driver
    participant DriverUI as Driver Dashboard
    participant TransporterAPI as Transporter API
    participant BookingAPI as Booking API
    participant DB as Database
    actor Farmer
    participant FarmerUI as Farmer Dashboard

    Driver->>TransporterAPI: PATCH live location
    TransporterAPI->>DB: Update transporter profile coordinates

    Driver->>DriverUI: Mark picked up
    DriverUI->>BookingAPI: POST status = picked_up
    BookingAPI->>DB: Validate location near pickup
    BookingAPI->>DB: Update booking + status history
    BookingAPI-->>DriverUI: Pickup confirmed

    Driver->>TransporterAPI: Send tracking updates while moving
    TransporterAPI->>DB: Save latest location
    DriverUI->>BookingAPI: POST tracking update
    BookingAPI->>DB: Save tracking record

    FarmerUI->>BookingAPI: GET tracking details
    BookingAPI->>DB: Read booking + tracking history
    BookingAPI-->>FarmerUI: Route and current delivery state

    Driver->>DriverUI: Mark delivered
    DriverUI->>BookingAPI: POST status = delivered
    BookingAPI->>DB: Validate location near dropoff
    BookingAPI->>DB: Update booking delivered
    BookingAPI->>DB: Trigger payment release / payout update
    BookingAPI-->>DriverUI: Delivery confirmed
    BookingAPI-->>FarmerUI: Final trip state available
```

## 6. Booking State Diagram

Description: Shows the lifecycle states a booking can move through in the backend.

```mermaid
stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> pending_payment
    pending_payment --> confirmed : successful payment
    pending_payment --> cancelled : cancellation / invalidation
    confirmed --> accepted : driver accepts
    confirmed --> declined : driver declines event recorded
    accepted --> picked_up : driver at pickup
    picked_up --> in_transit : trip progression
    in_transit --> delivered : driver at dropoff
    delivered --> completed : completion / payout release finalization
    cancelled --> [*]
    completed --> [*]
```

## 7. Payment State Diagram

Description: Shows how a payment record progresses from initiation to held funds and final release.

```mermaid
stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> pending
    pending --> stk_push_sent : STK initiated
    stk_push_sent --> paid_held : callback success
    stk_push_sent --> failed : callback failure
    stk_push_sent --> cancelled : user / provider cancellation
    paid_held --> released : delivery completed
    failed --> [*]
    cancelled --> [*]
    released --> [*]
```

## 8. Entity Relationship Diagram

Description: Shows the main persistent entities and how they relate in the database.

```mermaid
erDiagram
    CUSTOM_USER ||--o{ BOOKING : creates
    CUSTOM_USER ||--o{ BOOKING : assigned_to
    CUSTOM_USER ||--|| TRANSPORTER_PROFILE : owns
    TRANSPORTER_PROFILE ||--o{ VEHICLE : owns
    VEHICLE ||--o{ BOOKING : used_for
    BOOKING ||--o{ BOOKING_STATUS_HISTORY : records
    BOOKING ||--o{ TRACKING_UPDATE : has
    CUSTOM_USER ||--o{ TRACKING_UPDATE : sends
    BOOKING ||--|| PAYMENT : has
    PAYMENT ||--|| TRANSPORTER_PAYOUT : releases_to
    PAYMENT ||--o{ PAYMENT_STATUS_HISTORY : records
    CUSTOM_USER ||--o{ PAYMENT : pays
    CUSTOM_USER ||--o{ PAYMENT : receives
    CUSTOM_USER ||--o{ TRANSPORTER_PAYOUT : receives

    CUSTOM_USER {
        int id
        string phone_number
        string email
        string role
        bool is_email_verified
    }

    TRANSPORTER_PROFILE {
        int id
        int user_id
        string company_name
        decimal current_latitude
        decimal current_longitude
        datetime last_location_update
    }

    VEHICLE {
        int id
        int transporter_id
        string registration_number
        string vehicle_type
        decimal capacity_kg
        bool is_available
    }

    BOOKING {
        int id
        int farmer_id
        int transporter_id
        int vehicle_id
        string produce_name
        decimal weight_kg
        decimal quoted_price
        string status
        string payment_status
    }

    BOOKING_STATUS_HISTORY {
        int id
        int booking_id
        string status
        string notes
        datetime created_at
    }

    TRACKING_UPDATE {
        int id
        int booking_id
        int transporter_id
        decimal latitude
        decimal longitude
        decimal speed_kph
        datetime created_at
    }

    PAYMENT {
        int id
        int booking_id
        int farmer_id
        int transporter_id
        decimal amount_kes
        string status
        string mpesa_receipt_number
    }

    TRANSPORTER_PAYOUT {
        int id
        int booking_id
        int transporter_id
        int payment_id
        decimal amount_kes
        string status
    }

    PAYMENT_STATUS_HISTORY {
        int id
        int payment_id
        string status
        string notes
        datetime created_at
    }
```

